;; Count-round fixture (docs/incremental.md §6.2, M0): the TEMP-SPLIT case.
;; The rule stages through a temp ((h Y) is interned before (g id) can
;; emit); the two instantiations (e 1 2) and (e 2 2) agree on Y, so a
;; NARROW residue temp {Y} would collapse them to one row and undercount g.
;; The counted flavor's instantiation-injective wide temp {X, Y} keeps
;; both.  Hand-verified sidecar contents after (recount):
;;   e rows      -> input=1 (0,0)
;;   h (h 2)     -> (nonrec 2, rec 0)   (one interned instance, two derivations)
;;   g ((h 2))   -> (nonrec 2, rec 0)   (both instantiations reach the residue)

table (e int int)
struct (h int)
table (g h)

rule
(e 1 2)
(e 2 2)

rule
(e X Y)
-->
(g (h Y))
